{#- ============================================================
    lang-dropdown.njk — the language picker, in ONE place

    Lived inside layouts/base.njk until 2026-08-15, which meant the
    landing page could not use it without importing a whole layout.
    So the landing page kept its own bare .lang-toggle buttons — and
    when 7b724c3 rescoped the CSS to `.lang-dropdown-list .lang-toggle`
    to unify the picker, those buttons silently lost every style and
    rendered as default browser chrome. Nobody saw it for weeks
    because production was still serving an older build.

    One definition, imported by both, is what stops that recurring.

    The switch itself is still main.js's .lang-toggle click handler:
    langSwap + cookie + navigate. This only draws the open/closed list
    around it, and main.js binds any .lang-dropdown on the page, so a
    new consumer needs no JavaScript.

    modifier — "up" makes the list unfurl UPWARD. The landing page
    puts the picker at the bottom of a viewport that is locked to
    100% height with overflow:hidden, so a downward list would open
    off-screen and be clipped away entirely.
    ============================================================ -#}
{#- NAMES IN THE LIST, THE CODE ON THE BUTTON (Chase, 2026-10-08, and
    2026-10-12: "the actual pillbox to still show the language code"). The
    button is one width whatever the code, so the bar never shifts; after a
    switch, the old code rolls out and the new one in (main.js). Each name in
    its own language (i18n/<l>.json `name`). -#}
{% macro langDropdown(modifier="") %}
<div class="lang-dropdown{% if modifier %} {{ modifier }}{% endif %}">
  <button type="button" class="lang-dropdown-trigger" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false"><span class="lang-dropdown-label" data-code="{{ lang | upper }}">{{ lang | upper }}</span></button>
  <ul class="lang-dropdown-list" role="listbox">
    {#- activeLangs: offering a language that was not built is a menu item
       that 404s. -#}
    {%- for l in activeLangs %}
    <li role="option" aria-selected="{{ 'true' if l == lang else 'false' }}">
      {%- if l == lang %}
      <span class="lang-dropdown-current" lang="{{ l }}">{{ i18n[l].name or (l | upper) }}</span>
      {%- else %}
      <button type="button" class="lang-toggle" data-lang="{{ l }}" data-target="{{ page.url | langSwap(l) }}" lang="{{ l }}">{{ i18n[l].name or (l | upper) }}</button>
      {%- endif %}
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
